  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In adiabatic process, slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;graph is given as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>d</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>d</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mfrac><mtext>P</mtext><mtext>V</mtext></mfrac></math>.<br /><br />For a given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;graph, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>slope</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi></math></p><p><br />From the given graph,<br /><math><mrow><msub><mrow><mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"><mrow><mtext>slope</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#62;</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>slope</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub></mrow></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;<math><mrow><msub><mi>&#947;</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#62;</mo> <msub> <mi>&#947;</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Therefore, plot <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> should correspond to <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mi>&#947;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1.</mn><mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and plot <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> should correspond to <math> <mrow> <mtext>He</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mi>&#947;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1.</mn><mn>6</mn><mn>7</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>.</p>",
